import json
F = []
def q(id, sev, where, finding, why, fix): F.append({"id": id, "severity": sev, "where": where, "finding": finding, "why": why, "fix": fix})

q("Q01", "critical", "60-acute-route.json DM-ACU-ROUTE-27/27B/27C/28/28B/28C (atLeast pregnant | postpartum_weeks); build.py run_vignette pregnancyUnknownCounts (line ~399)",
  "A woman who answers 'not pregnant' and has no postpartum answer is treated as not postpartum. pregnancyUnknownCounts only fires when the pregnancy answer is missing; once pregnant=false is recorded, the postpartum arm is 'insufficient' and nothing names the gap. Evaluator: P1 woman 30, pregnant false, postpartum blank, 170/115 -> nothing; P2 same, 150/100 with hypertensive_organ_damage (seizure / visual loss) -> nothing (district identical); P3 same, 150/100, drowsy -> nothing; Q01b known type 2, 'not pregnant', 170/115 -> DM-ACT-REFER-BP-01 same_day only. With postpartum_weeks=2 recorded the same patients get ROUTE-28 / 28B / 28C immediate. Grid (r7/grid7b.py, women 30, 'not pregnant, postpartum blank'): 228 cells >=160/110 with no interrupt, 114 organ-damage cells with no interrupt, 16 drowsy >=140/90 cells with no interrupt, 222 cells >=140/90 with nothing same-day.",
  "A recently delivered woman truthfully answers 'not pregnant'. UCG-PE-04: pre-eclampsia 'can present as late as 4-6 weeks postpartum'. Treating an unasked postpartum question as 'no' is rule 2, and postpartum eclampsia is the case L03/L13/L15 were meant to close.",
  "Extend the pregnancyUnknownCounts semantics to the postpartum arm: when sex is female, pregnancy_possible is not false and postpartum_weeks is not recorded, evaluate the criterion with the postpartum arm as possible, fire, and name 'postpartum_weeks' as the gap (or have the engine ask 'birth in the last 6 weeks?' whenever pregnant=false is recorded). Window from REF-DM-PREG-PE-POSTPARTUM (UCG-PE-04). Vignettes P1, P2, P3; add a 'not pregnant, postpartum blank' state to the build grid.")

q("Q02", "critical", "k_r6.py DM_ANY (dm_type_recorded in type_1, type_2, unclassified, other); every acute rule using it (02, 07, 21, 21B, 22, 26, 30, 34 ...)",
  "Gestational diabetes is not 'has diabetes'. R6 L11 asked for dm_type_recorded 'gestational' to be in the shared list; DM_ANY omits it. Evaluator: P9 pregnant 30 weeks, dm_type_recorded gestational, status blank, vomiting, glucose 9, blood ketones 3.5 -> NOTHING; P9b same at district with urine ketones 3+ -> NOTHING; P12 GDM recorded, list blank, glucose 3.2 -> NOTHING. With dm_status known added (P10) the rules work. Grid7b: 62 GDM cells with ketones 3.0+/3+ and no interrupt, 24 GDM cells with glucose 3.5 and nothing.",
  "The shared list exists because one box is ticked without another (L04); a recorded gestational type with a blank status box is the same situation. Ketoacidosis in pregnancy occurs at glucose values below the ROUTE-02 'raised glucose' arm, so the glucose arm does not rescue her. Silence on blood ketones 3.5 in a pregnant woman with diabetes is a missed emergency.",
  "Add 'gestational' to DM_ANY's dm_type_recorded list (one line in k_r6.py). Add vignettes P9, P9b, P12 and a GDM profile to the build grid.")

q("Q03", "critical", "k_r6.py ACUTE_ORDER (28, 28B, 28C ranked above 02, 30, 03, 14, 29, 17, 11, 24); displays of ROUTE-28/28B/28C under pregnancyUnknownCounts",
  "When a pregnancy rule fires only because pregnancy is unanswered, it still takes the interrupt over measured emergencies, and its display asserts 'Pregnant or within 6 weeks of birth ... severe pre-eclampsia or eclampsia'. Evaluator: O1 woman 48, known type 2, drowsy, meter HI, BP 150/92, pregnancy blank -> interrupt ROUTE-28C (eclampsia), ROUTE-14 (hyperosmolar) folded; O2 woman 48, stroke signs, drowsy, 200/115, glucose 9 -> interrupt ROUTE-28, ROUTE-17 (stroke) and 24 folded; O6 woman 45, blood ketones 3.5, glucose 25, vomiting, 165/112 -> interrupt ROUTE-28, ROUTE-02 (DKA) folded; O3 woman 72 with pregnancy_possible not supplied -> same as O1. Grid7b: 722 cells where a pregnancy-unknown interrupt is shown over a folded measured emergency (02, 14, 17, 11, 24, 29, 30, 03).",
  "The shown interrupt is what the team acts on first. Naming eclampsia in a 48-year-old with a hyperosmolar state or a stroke sends her down the wrong pathway (obstetric triage, magnesium) while the time-critical one is a folded line. The display claims a fact (pregnant) the record does not hold: rule 10.",
  "In the fold, rank any rule whose criterion was met only through pregnancyUnknownCounts after every other immediate rule (the build knows this: it appends the 'pregnant' gap). Give those rules a display variant for the unknown case: 'Pregnancy not recorded: ask now. If pregnant or within 6 weeks of birth: ...'. Add an order invariant to the build: no pregnancy-unknown interrupt above a measured emergency. Vignettes O1, O2, O6.")

q("Q04", "critical", "build.py designb_rules (line 574: appliesTo.pregnancy = 'pregnant' if any predicate reads 'pregnant'); designb/pack-manifest.draft.json rows DM-ACU-ROUTE-27, 27B, 27C, 28, 28B, 28C",
  "The Design B manifest declares appliesTo {pregnancy: 'pregnant'} for all six pregnancy BP rules, and carries no pregnancyUnknownCounts flag (0 occurrences). The catalog criteria have a postpartum arm (pregnant OR postpartum_weeks <= 6) and rely on pregnancyUnknownCounts for the unanswered case. Observed: manifest row DM-ACU-ROUTE-28B 'appliesTo': {'ageBands': None, 'pregnancy': 'pregnant'}; same for 27, 27B, 27C, 28, 28C; the catalog 60-acute-route.json entries carry pregnancyUnknownCounts: true and no appliesTo.",
  "appliesTo.pregnancy is the field an engine uses to decide whether a rule runs (it withholds not_pregnant items today). An engine honouring the manifest will not run these rules for a postpartum woman (pregnant=false, postpartum 2 weeks) or for a woman whose pregnancy is unanswered, which undoes L03, L13 and L15 in the artefact Phase 2 deploys; the reference evaluator never reads rule appliesTo, so the build cannot see it.",
  "Derive appliesTo from the criterion: a rule with a postpartum arm is 'any' (or a new value 'pregnant_or_postpartum'); emit pregnancyUnknownCounts in the manifest row; add a build assertion that each manifest row's appliesTo admits every vignette on which the catalog rule fires (DMV-111, DMV-119 would fail today).")

q("Q05", "critical", "60-acute-route.json DM-ACU-ROUTE-28C (and missing rule); DM-ACU-ROUTE-15 ageBands child/adolescent only",
  "Missing blood pressure and missing glucose are read as normal for drowsy adults outside the diabetes list. Evaluator: P7 pregnant 34 weeks, drowsy, BP not recorded (glucose 7) -> NOTHING (ROUTE-28C needs a BP; grid7b: 16 cells); 'pregnant drowsy glucose 6, BP not recorded' -> nothing; G10 adult 40, diabetes status blank, vomiting and drowsy, no glucose -> NOTHING; adult 'not_known' diabetes in coma, no glucose, district -> NOTHING. A child in the same state gets ROUTE-15 immediate ('capillary glucose now').",
  "Rule 2. A drowsy pregnant woman is eclampsia or hypoglycaemia until a BP and a glucose say otherwise; a drowsy or comatose adult of unknown diabetes status needs a glucose now (new diabetes presenting as DKA or a hyperosmolar state, or a low). The pack already accepts this logic for children (ROUTE-15) and for known diabetes (ROUTE-20, D-DM-37 item 1).",
  "Run ROUTE-15 at all ages ('drowsy or worse, no glucose on record: capillary glucose now'), sourced as D-DM-37 item 1 is. Add a 28C companion: pregnant or within REF-DM-PREG-PE-POSTPARTUM weeks (unknown counts), drowsy or worse, BP not recorded -> immediate 'BP and glucose now' (UCG-PE-02). Vignettes P7, G10.")

q("Q06", "critical", "60-acute-route.json DM-ACU-ROUTE-27B (when, notWhen, display)",
  "27B tells the clinician 'gestational or chronic hypertension. Review the blood-pressure plan today and aim below 140/90' whenever the strip is negative or trace, whatever else is recorded. It does not read hypertensive_symptoms (headache, blurred vision, nausea or vomiting) or hypertensive_organ_damage. Evaluator: P4 34 weeks, 150/100, headache and blurred vision, protein negative -> ROUTE-27B same_day only; P5 / L-B7 34 weeks, organ damage, protein negative -> ROUTE-28B immediate AND ROUTE-27B 'gestational or chronic hypertension' beside it. Grid7b: 76 pregnant/postpartum cells >= 140/90 with headache and no interrupt.",
  "27B's own cited source (UCG-CHTN-03) says 'if not controlled or any sign of pre-eclampsia: refer to hospital'; headache and visual disturbance are listed by UCG-HTN-03 under hypertensive encephalopathy. A negative strip does not exclude pre-eclampsia (UCG-PE-02: 'any degree of hypertension with evidence of organ dysfunction'). Labelling her 'gestational hypertension, review the plan' is rule 10 and could delay referral of imminent eclampsia.",
  "27B notWhen hypertensive_symptoms present or hypertensive_organ_damage present. Add a rule: pregnant or postpartum (unknown counts), BP >= REF-DM-PREG-BP-SBP/DBP, hypertensive_symptoms present -> refer to hospital today (UCG-CHTN-03), or interrupt if the CSO reads UCG 2023 16.3.7's symptom list that way; quote that list into the research table first. Vignettes P4, P5.")

q("Q07", "major", "k_r6.py ACUTE_ORDER; evaluator fold (build.py 448-450); DM-ACU-ROUTE-03, -20, -32, -05 displays; DMV-100",
  "Interrupts whose action is a measurement outrank interrupts whose action is 'route now', and the folded item's action is not carried. Grid7 (82,160 male cells): ROUTE-03 shown over folded 14/11/24 in 1,592 cells, ROUTE-20 over folded 02/24/25/29/30 in 1,536, ROUTE-32 over folded 02/30 in 264. Evaluator: SGLT2, vomiting, glucose 35 -> interrupt ROUTE-03 'check ketones even if glucose is normal', ROUTE-14 folded; L-C10 child type 1, vomiting, urine ketones 3+, no glucose -> interrupt ROUTE-32 'capillary glucose and ketones now', ROUTE-02 'suspected ketoacidosis. Route now' folded; DMV-100 (asserted) 230/130 drowsy -> interrupt ROUTE-20 'capillary glucose now', ROUTE-29 folded; K1 DKA with potassium 6.8 -> ROUTE-05 ('ECG monitoring') folded.",
  "Checking a glucose first in a drowsy patient is right, but the banner then reads as a test, not a transfer. For the SGLT2 patient at 35 the message is wrong on its face. Hyperkalaemia 6.5 or more needs its own concurrent action (ECG monitoring), not a line of reasons.",
  "Specify in the semantics that the interrupt carries every folded item's proposal (route, ECG) as actions, not only reasons; move ROUTE-03 below 14 and 11, ROUTE-32 below 02 and 30; and add a build invariant: when any folded item proposes acute.route, the shown interrupt's actions include it.")

q("Q08", "major", "build.py check_acute_grid / k_grid.check (double counter) and k_grid floor dimensions; decisions D-DM-41 'recommended' text",
  "The '0 double' result cannot be anything else: run_vignette relabels every immediate after the first as 'folded' before k_grid counts urgency == 'immediate'. Observed: 1,371 of the 4,608 build cells still meet two or more interrupt rules (1,138 x2, 225 x3, 8 x4; R6 counted 1,155). The floor grid has no urine ketones 2+/3+, acetone, dehydration, abdominal pain, acute illness, meter LO, numeric glucose 33.3+, laboratory glucose, older_adult band, district site, female sex or pregnancy, BP, potassium or chest pain; D-DM-41's recommended text asks the CSO to sign an acetone row the grid cannot test. Every regression in Q01-Q06 sits outside it.",
  "The CSO is asked to sign 'a table the build enforces'; most of the acute surface is not enforced, and the double check gives false assurance.",
  "Replace the double counter with an order invariant (Q03, Q07). Add the dimensions above; r7/grid7.py (82,160 cells, 0 cells below the reviewer's floor, which re-uses the pack's own thresholds) and r7/grid7b.py (pregnancy/BP, 12,000 cells) can be lifted into k_grid. Make D-DM-41's text list exactly the rows k_grid.floor encodes.")

q("Q09", "major", "60-acute-route.json DM-ACU-ROUTE-24 (L05 widening) and DM-ACU-ROUTE-25",
  "The dehydration and acetone arms interrupt for any diabetes, including metformin-only or diet-only, and do not stand down on a normal blood ketone. Evaluator: G5 type 2 on metformin, dehydrated, glucose 7, blood ketones 0.2 -> ROUTE-24 immediate 'route now, whatever the glucose'; G5b same at district, urine negative -> same; G6 acetone, glucose 7, blood ketones 0.2 -> same; child type 1 dehydrated, glucose 7, blood ketones 0.2 -> ROUTE-25 immediate 'suspected ketoacidosis'. Grid7: 48 metformin/diet cells (glucose 7, ketones normal) interrupt.",
  "R6 L05 asked for dehydration and drowsiness at any glucose for insulin, SGLT2 and type 1 users. Gastroenteritis in a metformin-treated adult with a normal glucose and a measured normal ketone is not an interrupt (rule 9), and 'suspected ketoacidosis' with blood ketones 0.2 is rule 10.",
  "Keep drowsiness and Kussmaul for all diabetes; limit the dehydration and acetone arms of 24 to type 1, insulin and SGLT2 (and dehydration in children with diabetes for 25); stand both arms down on bohb < REF-DM-ACU-KETONE-LOW; send the rest to ROUTE-13-style same day. Vignettes G5, G6.")

q("Q10", "major", "build.py pregnancyUnknownCounts on DM-ACU-ROUTE-27 and -28; DMV-119",
  "Every woman whose pregnancy is unrecorded gets a pregnancy BP action. Evaluator: O5 woman 45, known type 2, 145/92, routine visit -> ROUTE-27 same_day 'urine protein today'; O4 same at 165/100, no symptoms -> ROUTE-28 immediate 'Pregnant ... acute severe hypertension. Route now'; DMV-119 asserts the interrupt for 170/115. A man with the same readings gets nothing acute (165/100) or a same-day referral (above 200/110).",
  "Hypertension is common in women attending a diabetes clinic, and the pregnancy question is often not asked at routine visits; the result is a same-day order on most hypertensive women and interrupts on many (rule 9). The question that resolves it takes seconds.",
  "When the rule fires only through unknown pregnancy, issue one prompt 'Pregnancy not recorded: ask now' (urgency of the underlying rule only once the answer is yes), and put the choice to the CSO under D-DM-36. Vignettes O4, O5.")

q("Q11", "major", "40-stratify.json tgt_hba1c_tight (k_r6.py: notWhen [], label 'good health, low risk of lows')",
  "The tight target copies none of the general target's stops. Evaluator: tier 'tight', glibenclamide, a low needing help in the last year, HbA1c 6.9 -> targets include tgt_hba1c_tight (below 6.5%) while DM-ACT-RX-10 fires 'relax the target for now' and the hypoglycaemia flags fire; without the tier the same patient gets tgt_hba1c_relaxed. Tier 'tight' with eGFR 40 -> tgt_hba1c_tight and tgt_hba1c_ckd (6.5 to 8.0) together.",
  "REF-DM-CTRL-HBA1C-TIGHT's own quote (ADA Rec 6.4) limits the lower goal to people with 'low treatment risks (e.g., hypoglycemia)'; the label promises that and the predicates do not test it (rule 10). A 6.5% goal beside a recent severe low on a sulfonylurea points toward more treatment.",
  "Give tgt_hba1c_tight the same relaxed-reason stop as tgt_hba1c_general (frailty, cognitive impairment, hypo_worst_12m, hypo_awareness_score), so the relaxed target supersedes; decide whether tight supersedes tgt_hba1c_ckd. Vignette: tight + needed-help low -> tgt_hba1c_relaxed.")

q("Q12", "major", "60-acute-route.json DM-ACU-ROUTE-23 (display, proposal test.ketones) at district sites",
  "At a district site (no lab.ketones_blood) ROUTE-23 asks for 'blood ketones today', and only a blood ketone clears it. Evaluator: L-C4 8-year-old type 1, vomiting, glucose 7, urine ketones negative, district -> ROUTE-23 same_day; C1 abdominal pain, glucose 6, district -> same. No referral or contact instruction is given.",
  "Rule 8: the district clinician gets a test they cannot do and no reachable next step.",
  "Site-aware display or a second arm: where blood ketones are unavailable, 'contact the diabetes team today / refer today to a site that can measure blood ketones' (ISPAD sick-day guidance, the source already in ROUTE-23's notes).")

q("Q13", "major", "60-acute-route.json DM-ACU-ROUTE-28B (k_r6.py: all=[hypertensive_organ_damage] only)",
  "28B never tests blood pressure, though its label says 'beside a raised pressure' and its display 'severe pre-eclampsia'. Evaluator: pregnant 30 weeks, organ-damage box ticked, BP 118/76 -> ROUTE-28B immediate 'severe pre-eclampsia'; woman 44, known type 2, pregnancy blank, organ-damage box, BP 118/76 -> ROUTE-28B immediate with the gap 'pregnant'.",
  "UCG-PE-02 requires 'any degree of hypertension'; a normotensive woman with pulmonary oedema or confusion needs routing, but not under that name (rule 10). The organ-damage box is also used outside pregnancy.",
  "Add BP >= REF-DM-PREG-BP-SBP or DBP to 28B; with BP not recorded, fire and name 'bp_systolic' as the gap (seizures in pregnancy must not wait for a cuff).")

q("Q14", "major", "60-acute-route.json DM-ACU-ROUTE-34 (when, display)",
  "ROUTE-34 fires when ketones were never measured and says 'with ketones below the danger range: tablets cannot be kept down'. Evaluator: type 2, vomiting, glucose 28, no ketone result -> ROUTE-34 same_day beside ROUTE-01 and -19; adult type 1 on insulin, vomiting, glucose 24, urine negative -> ROUTE-23 + ROUTE-34 'tablets'; L-C11 14-year-old type 1 on insulin -> ROUTE-34 'tablets' under the ROUTE-04 interrupt; SGLT2, vomiting, glucose 35, no ketones -> ROUTE-34 beside ROUTE-01, -19 and the interrupt.",
  "A missing ketone result is shown as a reassuring one (rule 2, rule 10); 'tablets' is wrong for insulin users and children. Harm is limited because ROUTE-01/19 ask for ketones in the same output.",
  "Require a ketone result in ROUTE-34's criterion (urine neg/trace/1+ or a blood ketone below REF-DM-ACU-KETONE-LOW), and word the display by therapy ('oral medicines or insulin plan cannot be kept to'). Stand it down under any interrupt.")

q("Q15", "major", "k_grid.floor rows for vomiting with a high glucose; DM-ACU-ROUTE-34 scope (vomiting only)",
  "The floor treats type 1 and type 2 the same when vomiting with a high glucose: same_day. Evaluator: adult type 1 on insulin, vomiting, glucose 24, urine negative -> same_day only (23, 34); C2 child type 1, vomiting, glucose 25, urine negative, district -> ROUTE-04 interrupt (children are covered). G4 75-year-old type 2, glucose 30, ketones negative, acutely ill (no vomiting, no dehydration ticked) -> nothing acute (GLU-02 dark).",
  "Vomiting in type 1 on insulin is the sick-day red flag in ISPAD 2022 and the JBDS sick-day guidance, and urine strips under-read early ketonaemia (REF-DM-VAL-URINE-KETONE). ROUTE-34's own rationale ('the hyperosmolar state can develop without ketones', independent of D-DM-38) applies equally to an older adult with an infection; reading vomiting only is narrower than the reason given.",
  "Put two rows to the CSO under D-DM-41: type 1 or insulin, vomiting, glucose >= REF-DM-ACU-KETONE-TEST-GLU, no blood ketone -> immediate or hospital today per ISPAD 2022 / JBDS sick-day text (quote it into the research table first); and extend ROUTE-34's 'any' to acute_illness_current for older adults, sourced to the JBDS HHS guideline.")

q("Q16", "major", "DM-ACU-ROUTE-21B, -22, -30, -23 (no pregnancy arm)",
  "Pregnancy does not change any ketone rule. Evaluator: P11 pregnant with type 1, vomiting, glucose 9, blood ketones 1.0 -> ROUTE-21B same_day 'recheck within 2 hours'; P11c pregnant with type 1, abdominal pain, glucose 9, blood ketones 2.0 -> ROUTE-22 same_day.",
  "Ketoacidosis in pregnancy develops faster and at lower glucose, and threatens the fetus; the pack has no source on it.",
  "Add the JBDS-IP guideline on DKA in pregnancy (2017) and the relevant UCG 2023 chapter 16 text to the research table, and let the CSO decide whether pregnancy raises 21B/22 to same-day-with-obstetrics or immediate. No threshold from memory.")

q("Q17", "major", "catalog/60-acute-route.json, catalog/00 semantics.interrupt, catalog/40-stratify.json, designb/pack-manifest.draft.json",
  "The interrupt order exists only in build.py/k_r6.py: catalog/00 says 'the first in ACUTE_ORDER' but no file under catalog/, designb/ or clerking-v2/ contains the list or a per-rule rank (grep: 0). The Design B manifest still carries no time scope ('at this encounter': 0; L17), no supersedes, no fold.",
  "Phase 2 ports the catalog; it cannot reproduce the fold, so the one-interrupt behaviour that the grid enforces is not shipped.",
  "Emit x.acuteRank on every immediate rule (and the order list in catalog/00), carry acuteRank, supersedes and recordedScope into the manifest, and assert in the build that the shipped order equals ACUTE_ORDER.")

minors = [
 ("Q18", "60-acute-route.json DM-ACU-ROUTE-03 display", "Display still 'vomiting, in pain or breathing deeply ... even if glucose is normal' after L05 added dehydration and drowsiness; L-S1 (drowsy) and the glucose-35 patient see it.", "Rule 10.", "Display from the label; drop 'even if glucose is normal' when a glucose >= REF-DM-ACU-DKA-GLU is recorded."),
 ("Q19", "60-acute-route.json DM-ACU-ROUTE-32 display", "Still 'capillary glucose and ketones now' when ketones are recorded (L-C10, urine 3+); L22 changed the proposal only.", "Rule 10.", "Display 'capillary glucose now'."),
 ("Q20", "60-acute-route.json DM-ACU-ROUTE-07 display", "Metformin listed, type blank, 3.6 (L-H12) -> 'if the medicines are not known'; the medicines are known, the type is not.", "Rule 10 (L11c partly fixed).", "Say 'or the type is not recorded'."),
 ("Q21", "60-acute-route.json DM-ACU-ROUTE-24/-25 notWhen hypo (<3.0 only)", "Hypoglycaemic patients at 3.0 to 3.9 still carry a folded 'suspected ketoacidosis. Route now' (L-C3, L-H1, L-A3).", "L12 partly fixed; misleading reason under the hypo interrupt.", "Stand 24/25 down below REF-DM-HYPO-L1 as R6 proposed."),
 ("Q22", "acute lane, same-day items under an interrupt", "30,886 of 82,160 grid7 cells show same-day items beside an interrupt (01, 19, 23, 34, 27, DM-ACT-REFER-BP-01): L-C11 has 01, 23, 34 under ROUTE-04; DMV-100/O2 show BP-01 'same-day referral' under the interrupt.", "'Today' beside 'now' (L21 partly fixed).", "Fold same-day acute items into the interrupt as well, or stand them down when an interrupt is met."),
 ("Q23", "build.py run_vignette gaps", "DMV-119: gap 'pregnant' is recorded for ROUTE-27 although ROUTE-27 is suppressed (stops on >=160/110); the gap is appended before notWhen is applied.", "Gap list overstates.", "Append the gap only when the rule fires."),
 ("Q24", "01-features.json hypertensive_symptoms display", "Still lists 'blurred vision'; UCG-HTN-03 puts visual disturbance (and severe headache) under hypertensive encephalopathy.", "L10 partly fixed.", "Move visual disturbance to hypertensive_organ_damage, per UCG 2023 4.1.6.1."),
 ("Q25", "build.py preg_state; k_grid / vignettes", "No grid row or vignette supplies pregnancy_possible; a 72-year-old woman without it gets ROUTE-28C and every target withheld (O3). The pack does not state the age band the platform must use.", "Behaviour depends on an unstated platform parameter.", "State the band in catalog/00 (CSO), and give the older-women and adolescent vignettes pregnancy_possible explicitly."),
 ("Q26", "60-acute-route.json DM-ACU-ROUTE-13, -20 displays", "Still 'Diabetes (or on insulin or a sulfonylurea)' after the DM_ANY change.", "Rule 10 drift.", "Display from the label."),
 ("Q27", "40-stratify.json tgt_hba1c_ckd with general/relaxed/tight", "eGFR 40 -> two HbA1c targets at once (general 7.0 + CKD 6.5-8.0; tight 6.5 + CKD).", "Two goals for one measure.", "Decide supersedes for the CKD target."),
]
for id, where, finding, why, fix in minors: q(id, "minor", where, finding, why, fix)
json.dump(F, open("R7-review.json", "w"), indent=1, ensure_ascii=False)
print(len(F), {s: sum(1 for f in F if f["severity"] == s) for s in ("critical", "major", "minor")})
